      "entity": "husband of Chilonis",
      "scope": "explicitly stated",
      "claim": "Cleonymus is the husband of Chilonis.",
      "answer": "Cleonymus",
      "quote": "Chilonis (daughter of Leotychidas) Chilonis () was a Spartan princess, daughter of Leotychidas, wife of Cleonymus and mother of Areus II. She is known from Plutarch's \"Life of Pyrrhus\". Her much older husband Cleonymus, a son of Cleomenes II, had not been allowed to succeed to his father's throne because of his violent and tyrannical behaviour, and had spent many years away from Sparta as a soldier of fortune.",
      "original_document_number": 1
    },
    {
      "doc_id": "ramdocs-0158-581f7e1afea2:d01",
